UID:4686501624e6c767@nutcracker2026
DTSTAMP:20260914T010516Z
SEQUENCE:2026091401
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20261210T194500
SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:Thu. Dec. 10 · Call 6:00 PM · 7:00 PM–7:45 PM · Robinson
  Center\nMANDATORY — production week. CALL TIME 6:00 PM: dancers must 
 be checked in and backstage by then\, so arrive by 5:45 PM. BA: Call Tim
 e is the time dancers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minut
 es before Call Time.\nACT I Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair a
 nd Makeup.\nAll Casts are called unless a cast is named. SUBJECT TO CHAN
 GE — the BA master schedule\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal a
 re the official source. Master: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1
 xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\nCOSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP 
 for Artillery: Soldiers: Artillery\, Brigade\, Infantry — Costume (you
  provide): Black Seamless Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard Male Soldiers:
  Black T-shirt\, Black tights\; Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Ligh
 t Stage Makeup\; Hair: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides): W
 hite Gloves\; Prop (BA provides): Brown gun\nLight Stage Makeup Instruct
 ion Sheet:\n•  Powder matching skintone\n•  Light brown eye sh
 adow applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n•  Dark Brown/
 Black eyeliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n•  Blush on the 
 cheeks (be sure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in t
 he stage lights)\n•  Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may
  wear flesh tone tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guide
 lines:\n•  Handle costume pieces with care while changing to preven
 t damage to delicate fabrics\n•  Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in
  the event of costume damage at the point of discovery\, no matter how s
 ignificant\n•  Never throw costumes or accessories on the floor\, o
 r hang costumes by their elastic straps\n•  Refrain from sitting on
  the floor while in costume\n•  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, cl
 ean\, or launder any costume or accessory\n•  Never apply stage mak
 e-up while in costume and shall take great care to refrain from smudging
  make-up on costume during its removal\n•  Refrain from the use of 
 spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n•  Never wear any garmen
 t not assigned to cast member\n•  Do not handle or consume food or 
 beverage while in costume\, with the exception of water\n•  Do not 
 remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or from the theater\n
 •  Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces and wigs follow
 ing their use\n•  Return all headpieces to their assigned bags\n•
   Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wardrob
 e policies\n•  Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or any
 thing that may damage or stain costumes.
BEGIN:VALARM
TRIGGER:-PT1H
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Nutcracker in 1 hour
END:VALARM
END:VEVENT
